# The student and teacher sites and the db scripts read these. Locally the default is a
# SQLite file at data/lemmory.db, so you don't need a .env file to develop.
# For production, set these in Netlify on the student and teacher sites (see DEPLOY.md):
# DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-db.turso.io
# DATABASE_AUTH_TOKEN=...

# Only if your Netlify site names differ from DEPLOY.md (or you use your own domain):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TEACHER_URL=https://lemmory-teacher.netlify.app
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDENT_URL=https://lemmory-student.netlify.app
